# Testing and Traceability Rules

Every target-behavior test should reference at least one requirement or acceptance criterion in its test name, docstring, comment, or adjacent evidence record.

Verification order:
1. acceptance/targeted tests,
2. existing regression suite,
3. sanity/preflight checks when relevant.

If a legacy regression conflicts with an approved target spec, flag the conflict explicitly and update the regression only with documented rationale and traceability.
